      "text": "First, note that the first three stages each require 4 toothpicks. For the next stage, that will require 4 + 3 = 7 toothpicks. For the next stage after that, 7 + 3 = 10 toothpicks will be required. Seen in more mathematical terms, each stage has 3 more toothpicks than the previous stage. This can be expressed as a sequence, where the 1st term 4, the 2nd term 7, the 3rd term 10, the 4th term 13, and so on. The terms of the sequence, and the sum of all terms from the 1st to the 250th terms have an arithmetic sequence that can be found by finding the first term, the common difference, and the number of terms that makes up the sequence. The first term is 4, the common difference is 3, and the number of terms is 250. We can solve using the formula for arithmetic sequences where the first term is a1 and the common difference is d = n + a1. For this sequence, a1 = 4 and d = 3. Tn = a1 + (n-1) x d Substituting given values to the formula, 250 = 4 + (n-1) x 3 Solving for n, we find out that n = 90, since n starts at 1. With that, the sum of the sequence would be = 250 x (4+x(3))/2 = 3750, and the toothpicks required to fare the arrangement 250th stage would be equal. Tes, , , , , , , , , , , , , , , , \n  \\boxed{3750}\n\n[asy]\nsize(150);\ndefaultpen(linewidth(0.7));\nvoid drawSquare(pair A){\n\ndraw((A.x + 0.1,A.y)--(A.x + 0.9,A.y));\n\ndraw((A.x,A.y + 0.1)--(A.x,A.y + 0.9));\n\ndraw((A.x + 1,A.y + 0.1)--(A.x + 1,A.y + 0.9));\n\ndraw((A.x + 0.1,A.y + 1)--(A.x + 0.9,A.y + 1));\n}\n\nint k = 0;\n\nfor(int i = 1; i <= 3; ++i){\n\nfor(int j = 0; j < i; ++j){\n\ndrawSquare((k,0));\n\n++k;\n\n}\n\ndraw((k+0.1,0.5)--(k+0.9,0.5),EndArrow);\n\n++k;\n}\nlabel(\"$\\cdots$\",(k,0.5));\n[/asy]\n\nthe final answer is 3750",
