      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the number of toothpicks needed in the 250th stage of the pattern. We observe that each stage is a square with sides of length \\(i\\), where \\(i\\) is the stage number. We can determine the perimeter of this square to get the number of toothpicks.\n\nIn the first stage, the perimeter is \\(4\\) toothpicks. Each successive stage adds \\(4\\) toothpicks to the perimeter. Therefore, the number of toothpicks in the \\(n\\)th stage is given by the formula:\n\\[\n\\text{Toothpicks}_n = 4n\n\\]\n\nTo find the number of toothpicks in the 250th stage, we simply substitute \\(n = 250\\) into the formula:\n\\[\n\\text{Toothpicks}_{250} = 4 \\times 250 = 1000\n\\]\n\nWe can use Python to verify this result.\n```python\n# Number of stages\nn = 250\n\n# Formula to calculate the number of toothpicks in the nth stage\ntoothpicks = 4 * n\nprint(toothpicks)\n```\n```output\n1000\n```\nThe number of toothpicks necessary to create the arrangement for the 250th stage is \\(\\boxed{1000}\\).",
